\frametitle{Embedding Images with ViT}
\begin{splitcode}{%

\texttt{ViTEmbedder} wraps Google's Vision Transformer, trained on 14 million images across 21,843 classes --- it splits an image into patches and treats each one the way a language model treats a word.

Every image becomes a dense 768-number vector; unlike sparse TF-IDF, nearly every entry is non-zero and no single dimension has a name. Only the geometry matters.

}
\begin{lstlisting}[language=Python]
vit = ViTEmbedder()
(
    birds
    .select(c.filepath, c.label, c.vit)
)
\end{lstlisting}
\begin{codeoutput}
shape: (1555, 3)
filepath                   label     vit
"media/birds10/00000.png"  "canary"  [0.0179, -0.0305, 0.0577, ...]
"media/birds10/00001.png"  "canary"  [0.0248, -0.0453, 0.0796, ...]
"media/birds10/00002.png"  "canary"  [0.0506, -0.0245, 0.0628, ...]
...                        ...       ...

# each vit entry is a length-768 list
\end{codeoutput}
\end{splitcode}
